    {
      "id": "61cc2508fff24f6797b8994e94952452",
      "text": "Discipline is essential for great results",
      "source": {
        "book": "Collins-2001-Good-to-Great-Why-Some-Companies-Make-the-Leap...and-Others-Dont_",
        "chapter": 73
      },
      "weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "id": "c08d6827a0e841d4befc7816ecb0e2b6",
      "text": "Disciplined action without disciplined understanding of the three circles cannot produce sustained great results",
      "source": {
        "book": "Collins-2001-Good-to-Great-Why-Some-Companies-Make-the-Leap...and-Others-Dont_",
        "chapter": 73
      },
      "weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "id": "912a8b8ffc5749658cac3ad2a1c303fb",
      "text": "A culture of discipline is necessary for enduring success",
      "source": {
        "book": "Collins-2001-Good-to-Great-Why-Some-Companies-Make-the-Leap...and-Others-Dont_",
        "chapter": 73
      },
      "weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "id": "7c8c4590836644109511cecb270fa30b",
      "text": "Discipline is key to staying within one's three circles",
      "source": {
        "book": "Collins-2001-Good-to-Great-Why-Some-Companies-Make-the-Leap...and-Others-Dont_",
        "chapter": 75
      },
      "weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "id": "406b9b6967284ff1a2de8be0bab7ee9e",
      "text": "A great company is more likely to die of indigestion from too much opportunity than starvation from too little",
      "source": {
        "book": "Collins-2001-Good-to-Great-Why-Some-Companies-Make-the-Leap...and-Others-Dont_",
        "chapter": 75
      },
      "weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "id": "350c4cac60ed46f1b8ef4552df8c0932",
      "text": "The more an organization has the discipline to stay within its three circles, the more it will have attractive opportunities for growth",
      "source": {
        "book": "Collins-2001-Good-to-Great-Why-Some-Companies-Make-the-Leap...and-Others-Dont_",
        "chapter": 75
      },
      "weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "id": "bef5c8e852ab4dc4a8bba52bcb902619",
      "text": "Eliminate class distinctions and create a meritocracy",
      "source": {
        "book": "Collins-2001-Good-to-Great-Why-Some-Companies-Make-the-Leap...and-Others-Dont_",
        "chapter": 75
      },
      "weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "id": "f21bca88c22d415e943b9997af2b3bd2",
      "text": "Align management, labor, and financial interests",
      "source": {
        "book": "Collins-2001-Good-to-Great-Why-Some-Companies-Make-the-Leap...and-Others-Dont_",
        "chapter": 75
      },
      "weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "id": "d94f55470c264382b827cb5deb4b2c5d",
      "text": "Prioritize employee welfare and interests",
      "source": {
        "book": "Collins-2001-Good-to-Great-Why-Some-Companies-Make-the-Leap...and-Others-Dont_",
        "chapter": 75
      },
      "weight": 1.0
    },
    {
